- scope/store.py: SqliteScopeStore — versioned append-only policy records
  (engagement_id, policy_version), WAL + busy-timeout for concurrent
  API+worker access, tombstoning clear (history preserved), canonical
  fingerprint RECOMPUTED on read and compared against the recorded
  column (stored-vs-stored comparison misses in-place rule edits),
  ScopeStoreUnavailable on every failure path (fail closed).
- scope/registry.py: optional durable backend; store-present mode makes
  the store the read authority (fresh every get, cross-process visible)
  with the in-memory dict as write-through cache; attach_store() runtime
  upgrade writes existing cache through; no-store mode keeps the exact
  legacy single-process behavior (all existing callers untouched).
- scope/__init__.py: export SqliteScopeStore/ScopeStoreUnavailable/
  default_scope_store_path/policy round-trip.
- api/app.py: opt-in bootstrap via WEBPENT_SCOPE_STORE_PATH (or
  WEBPENT_SCOPE_STORE_ENABLED=1); init failure is FATAL (no silent
  in-memory downgrade when a shared authority was requested).
- tests/test_umdr41_scope_registry.py: 8 tests executing the directive's
  scenario with REAL subprocesses (A loads, B reads, A updates, B sees
  v2, restart, store failure raises, tampered record rejected, legacy
  behavior pinned, concurrent appends serialized).
